  What we've been seeing aren't commandments.  They're hints and tips.

  Marvin stated as the secret to his success is "keep breathing."  I
phrase it as "Dead characters rarely accomplish much." 


  The technical version is:

  1.  Don't die without wearing an amulet of life saving.


  Everything else is just working through problems.  So the second
commandment is:

  2.  Don't give up.  
      - When in danger or in doubt - take your hands off the keyboard.
        - Your fingers will kill your character if you let them.)

  Which brings us to the next few commandments, which focus on what's
necessary to win.
  3. Don't change alignment before being accepted for the Quest.
  4. Don't get thrown out of the Quest before completing it.
  5. Get and save seven candles.
  6. You Ascend by #offering the Amulet of Yendor on an appropriate 
     Altar on the Astral Plane.

  With the important stuff out of the way, let's go for general advice
commandments.

  - Run away!  Run away!
  - Elbereth early and often.
  - Pets, pets, pets.
  - Throw things from a distance.
  - Don't be burdened.  
    - The next speed down from slow is dead slow.
  - Try on every non-cursed piece of armor you find.
  - Early on forget 
    - enchanting, 
    - fountains, 
    - spell casting
    - identifying 
      - Monsters will identify emergency items by using them.

